PCRE2 for OpenVMS
=================

This is PCRE2 @VERSION@ (Perl-compatible regular expressions) built natively
for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from the unmodified PCRE2 release plus the patches in
the vms-pcre2 project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-pcre2

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  PCRE2 is distributed under the BSD licence with
the PCRE2 exception; see LICENCE.MD.  The API is described in PCRE2.TXT and
the test program in PCRE2TEST.TXT.

What is installed
-----------------
    PCRE2$ROOT:[INCLUDE]PCRE2.H        the PCRE2 API
    PCRE2$ROOT:[INCLUDE]PCRE2POSIX.H   the POSIX-style wrapper API
    PCRE2$ROOT:[LIB]PCRE2-8.OLB        8-bit library (object library)
    PCRE2$ROOT:[LIB]PCRE2-POSIX.OLB    POSIX wrapper (needs PCRE2-8.OLB)
    PCRE2$ROOT:[BIN]PCRE2TEST.EXE      PCRE2's test program

Only the 8-bit code unit width is built, with Unicode support.  There is
no JIT compiler: PCRE2's JIT (SLJIT) does not support OpenVMS.

Setting up
----------
The kit installs PCRE2$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define PCRE2$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:PCRE2$STARTUP.COM

Building a program against PCRE2
--------------------------------
    $ CC /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED) /INCLUDE=PCRE2$ROOT:[INCLUDE] -
         /DEFINE=PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH=8 myprog.c
    $ LINK myprog, PCRE2$ROOT:[LIB]PCRE2-8.OLB/LIBRARY

/NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED) is required: several PCRE2 function names are
longer than 31 characters, and they only match the library when both sides
are compiled with the same /NAMES.  The POSIX wrapper links with
PCRE2$ROOT:[LIB]PCRE2-POSIX.OLB/LIBRARY before PCRE2-8.OLB.

pcre2test
---------
    $ pcre2test :== $PCRE2$ROOT:[BIN]PCRE2TEST.EXE
    $ pcre2test "-C"

Upper-case options such as -C need double quotes, or
SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED: traditional DCL parsing lower-cases
unquoted arguments.
